window.TIMINGS=[
 {
  "li": 0,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "If an elevator's ropes snap, what actually stops it? Not the ropes. The rails.",
  "show": "If an elevator's *ropes snap,* what actually stops it? Not the ropes. [The rails.]",
  "start": 0.0,
  "end": 5.12
 },
 {
  "li": 1,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Early lifts were a platform on one rope. Rope breaks, and nothing's left holding it.",
  "show": "Early lifts were a platform on *one rope.* Rope breaks, and [nothing's left holding it.]",
  "start": 5.7,
  "end": 10.36
 },
 {
  "li": 2,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Eighteen fifty-four. Elisha Otis flips it around. The rope's pull keeps a spring bent, and the spring holds two catches in.",
  "show": "1854. Elisha Otis flips it around. The *rope's pull* keeps a spring bent, and the spring holds two *catches* in.",
  "start": 11.86,
  "end": 17.86
 },
 {
  "li": 2,
  "pi": 1,
  "say": "Rope breaks? The pull is gone, the spring snaps straight, and the catches jam into teeth on the rails.",
  "show": "Rope breaks? The pull is gone, the spring snaps straight, and the catches jam into [teeth on the rails.]",
  "start": 18.34,
  "end": 23.76
 },
 {
  "li": 2,
  "pi": 2,
  "say": "The failure itself fires the brake. Engineers call that fail-safe.",
  "show": "The failure itself fires the brake. Engineers call that [fail-safe.]",
  "start": 24.14,
  "end": 27.64
 },
 {
  "li": 3,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Modern lifts hang on several steel ropes, not one. They loop over a grooved motor wheel to a counterweight, so the motor only lifts the difference.",
  "show": "Modern lifts hang on several *steel ropes,* not one. They loop over a motor wheel to a [counterweight,] so the motor only lifts the difference.",
  "start": 27.64,
  "end": 35.34
 },
 {
  "li": 4,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "The motor's brake is fail-safe too. Springs squeeze it shut. Electricity pulls it open. Power cut? It clamps by itself.",
  "show": "The motor's brake is fail-safe too. *Springs* squeeze it shut. *Electricity* pulls it open. Power cut? It [clamps by itself.]",
  "start": 35.88,
  "end": 42.68
 },
 {
  "li": 5,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "But what if the car just goes too fast? Up top sits a governor: a wheel driven by a thin rope loop that moves with the car.",
  "show": "But what if the car just goes *too fast?* Up top sits a [governor:] a wheel driven by a thin *rope loop* that moves with the car.",
  "start": 43.14,
  "end": 50.2
 },
 {
  "li": 5,
  "pi": 1,
  "say": "Spin it faster, and weights inside swing out. First, they flip a switch that cuts the power. Still too fast? They lock the rope.",
  "show": "Spin it faster, and *weights* inside swing out. First, they flip a switch that *cuts the power.* Still too fast? They [lock the rope.]",
  "start": 50.54,
  "end": 57.84
 },
 {
  "li": 6,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Now the rope stops, but the car keeps going. That pulls a lever on the car, and wedges slide up between the car and the rails. Friction drags it to a stop.",
  "show": "Now the rope stops, but the car keeps going. That pulls a *lever* on the car, and [wedges] slide up between the car and the rails. Friction drags it to a stop.",
  "start": 58.78,
  "end": 67.26
 },
 {
  "li": 7,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Fast lifts use wedges that grip gradually, so you're slowed, not slammed. And buffers in the pit catch the rest.",
  "show": "Fast lifts use wedges that grip *gradually,* so you're [slowed, not slammed.] And *buffers* in the pit catch the rest.",
  "start": 67.78,
  "end": 74.1
 },
 {
  "li": 8,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "The weak spot? Everything waits on that thin rope.",
  "show": "The weak spot? Everything waits on [that thin rope.]",
  "start": 74.76,
  "end": 77.58
 },
 {
  "li": 8,
  "pi": 1,
  "say": "In nineteen forty-five, a bomber hit the Empire State Building. Falling debris cut car six's ropes, governor rope included.",
  "show": "In 1945, a *bomber* hit the Empire State Building. Falling debris cut car 6's ropes, [governor rope included.]",
  "start": 78.1,
  "end": 84.56
 },
 {
  "li": 8,
  "pi": 2,
  "say": "The wedges were fine. Nothing pulled them. Car six fell seventy-five floors. Its operator, Betty Lou Oliver, survived.",
  "show": "The wedges were *fine.* Nothing pulled them. Car 6 fell [75 floors.] Its operator, Betty Lou Oliver, *survived.*",
  "start": 84.56,
  "end": 91.86
 },
 {
  "li": 9,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "So the safety gear moved to the far side of the shaft, away from harm.",
  "show": "So the safety gear moved to the [far side of the shaft,] away from harm.",
  "start": 92.56,
  "end": 96.12
 },
 {
  "li": 10,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Newer codes added more: a brake for a car shooting upward, and a stop if it moves with the doors open.",
  "show": "Newer codes added more: a brake for a car *shooting upward,* and a stop if it moves with [the doors open.]",
  "start": 96.7,
  "end": 101.6
 },
 {
  "li": 11,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "And the latest systems drop the rope completely. A sensor reads the speed, and electronics fire the wedges directly. No rope left to cut.",
  "show": "And the latest systems *drop the rope* completely. A *sensor* reads the speed, and electronics fire the wedges directly. [No rope left to cut.]",
  "start": 102.14,
  "end": 109.3
 },
 {
  "li": 12,
  "pi": 0,
  "say": "Every machine you trust has layers like this. Follow for more videos like this.",
  "show": "Every machine you trust has layers like this. [Follow] for more videos like this.",
  "start": 109.9,
  "end": 113.64
 }
];
